From: mscharged-port
Subject: Give DWCControl the actual friend and match control records natively
Upstream-base: 7a6bf165d9f1c5914181c079c7d4bfa7204f3509
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility

DWCControl in dwc_main.c embeds the friend and match control records,
whose types only dwc_friend.c and dwc_match.c defined. It held them as a
Wii-sized u8 friendcnt[0x60] and a DWCMatchControlView that places the
fields dwc_main.c uses at their Wii offsets. Natively DWCFriendControl
needs 0xA8 bytes and DWCMatchControl 0x4E0 instead of 0x4A0, and every
viewed field moves (qr2Obj 0x10 -> 0x20, sbObj 0xE8 -> 0xF8, aidList
0x2E8 -> 0x2F8, ...). DWCi_FriendInit wrote 0x48 bytes over the start of
the match control, leaving a friend-control pointer where dwc_main.c
reads qr2Obj, and DWCi_MatchInit wrote 0x40 bytes into transinfo. After a
failed login, DWC_ShutdownFriendsMatch passed that pointer to
qr2_shutdown, which freed memory the network allocator never returned.

The three record types move verbatim into dwci_control.h, which
dwc_friend.c and dwc_match.c include in place of their definitions.
Natively dwc_main.c embeds the actual DWCFriendControl and uses
DWCMatchControl for its view, whose field names it already shares; the
Wii view and friendcnt array are unchanged.

